# Always commit and push after changes

After completing any coherent unit of work in this repository (feature, fix, config
change, docs), ALWAYS finish by committing and pushing — without waiting to be asked:

1. `git add -A`
2. `git commit -m "<what and why, one line>"` — use the repo-local identity already
   configured (`advillegas <74381111+advillegas@users.noreply.github.com>`); never
   invent a placeholder name or email.
3. `git push origin main`
4. `git push --quiet vault main` — mirror to the local vault (the ecosystem's own
   private remote). If the vault remote is missing, initialize it once with
   `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File bootstrap\vault.ps1 init`.
5. Confirm the push succeeded (`git status -sb` shows `main...origin/main` with no
   ahead/behind) and report the commit SHA.

Notes:

- One commit per coherent change-set; don't batch unrelated work into one commit.
- The remote is the private repo `advillegas/sentivue-oracle`. It must stay private.
- Never force-push unless explicitly asked; if a push is rejected, fetch and retry.
- If a push genuinely cannot complete (auth/network), say so explicitly at the end of
  the turn — never end a turn with silently unpushed commits.
- This applies to the Windows authoring machine. On the deployed (air-gapped) Mac,
  committing still applies; pushing obviously does not.
